repository-code: "https://github.com/Urielledezma/Behavioural-Finance-Studies"
abstract: >-
  Four independent projects in behavioural finance, written for the course
  Comportamiento en las Finanzas y Toma de Decisiones at ITESO, each with its
  own report, code, tests and results. The first, P01, checks the estimators
  used on real brokerage data against a known ground truth: it injects the
  disposition effect and overprecision into synthetic trading records at
  strengths fixed in advance, for eight scenarios, and tests whether the
  proportion-of-gains-realised estimator and the turnover regression recover
  them, including two confounds under which the disposition estimator fires
  with no bias present.
keywords:
  - behavioural finance
  - disposition effect
  - overconfidence
  - agent-based simulation
  - Monte Carlo
  - bootstrap
  - Python
